{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/1341418-small-town-demon","id":1341418,"title":"Small Town Demon","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Demon: The Descent"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-10-15T02:24:49-07:00","id":1341418,"title":"Small Town Demon","content":"Hey guys! I wanted to start up a chronicle where the pcs basically were all demons who were in a circle in New York or some other big american city, and after doing one big job that would really bring the machine down on them. Their agency helped them flee to a small town in Northern norway(24 k people when it comes to population size). I wante to know if the idea was functional, and if you can do a DTD game in a town of that size?<br /> <br /> Any ideas or tips for shit i can throw at them when they are in said town will also be welcome <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8100-caedus","name":"Caedus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"300"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-15T06:49:13-07:00","id":1341432,"title":"","content":"I've done this type of thing with other genres so I'll keep it as generic as possible:<br /> <br /> 1. There's already some antagonist there and the PCs are stepping on his/her/its home turf<br /> 2. One or more of the big city baddies followed them and harass them occasionally. Perhaps they themselves are looking to redeem themselves in the eyes of the big city baddies so can't really call in reinforcements.<br /> 3. Deal with small-time issues such as travelers sensing that something is weird about this town (hunters, heroes, etc.)<br /> 4. The God-Machine is already here and it was a plot to lure them to this town for something else entirely. (all the workings of an infinite God)<br /> 5. Perhaps some well-meaning preacher/pastor/priest type becomes a stigmatic after witnessing something the PCs do and ends up calling down an Angel or 2, starting a cult following against the PCs.<br /> 6. Having so many Demons might attract some specific spirits which in turn causes issues for the PCs.<br /> 7, Maybe they discover some long lost piece of the God-Machine and can't decide what it is or what to do with it, leading to some internal struggles within the group.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":14512,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14512-ghostdriver","user":"Ghostdriver","date":". 10-15-2019, 09:52 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14512-ghostdriver","name":"Ghostdriver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14512_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"41"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-15T16:41:37-07:00","id":1341519,"title":"","content":"Not to toot my own horn, but I did <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/825315-the-town-that-ran-like-clockwork-demon-actual-play\">a thing</a>.<br /> <br /> A town that big is still larger than what I had in mind for my own game, but to be fair one of the core conceits I had in mind for my game was that it was absolutely <i>infested</i> with Infrastructure. To an extent though, I think a small population can be an asset in Demon. It's harder to get lost in the crowd, so you have to be more conscious of playing to your Cover, while the God-Machine conversely can afford to be less subtle just due to how much easier it is to cover up weirdness when you have fewer people to influence. One of the benefits of being the System, really.<br /> <br /> Seeing as the premise of your game is that the players are trying to escape the God-Machine, however, I'd be inclined to go in the opposite direction to the one I went with (unless you want to use <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14512-ghostdriver\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar14512_2.gif');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"14512\" data-vbnamecard=\"14512\">Ghostdriver</a>'s suggestion that the town was actually a trap). That is to say, have relatively little Infrastructure, which will leave both the Demons strapped for resources as they struggle to locate Aether to drain, and allow you to play any Angels in pursuit as struggling to overcome their lack of support. Probably give the players a session or two to settle into the setting, make some friends, and maybe even deal with some mundane local issues with the help of their supernatural powers, and then start drawing in the God-Machine's pursuers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-15T17:55:40-07:00","id":1341530,"title":"","content":"The God-Machine in general is <i>great</i> for &quot;weird crap&quot;. But you don't need to limit yourself just to the Machine - feel free to populate the town with <i>other</i> dark secrets and mysteries. Tying into what Ghostdriver said, maybe there is some decaying Infrastructure that was used to seal some<i>thing</i> else. The Ring can uncover this, and decide whether to fortify the Infrastructure, destroy it, or suborn it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-16T11:42:15-07:00","id":1341667,"title":"","content":"so having demons in a small town is a workable idea <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Good to know<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8100-caedus","name":"Caedus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"300"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}